nsensus.", "watch": "A second independent or high-quality poll confirming the Democratic edge in the September surveys would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Ryan Zinke (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Montana's western district is an open seat after Republican Ryan Zinke's retirement, with Republican Aaron Flint facing Democrat Sam Forstag and a Libertarian also on the ballot. The district carries a five-point Republican lean, and most expert ratings land at Lean R, though two outlets call it a Tossup and two say Likely R.\n\nRecent polling shows the race essentially tied, with a Democratic-sponsored survey giving Forstag a two-point edge and an academic poll a one-point Republican edge. Fundraising is nearly even, though Flint benefits from substantially more outside spending. Prediction markets still price the Republican near 70 percent, suggesting the district's underlying lean matters more than the tight surveys. The forecast lands at a modest Republican edge with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3744, "margin": -1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3797, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3473, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3145, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2903, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3867, "margin": -2.0}]}